 |  6 MB  |  a minute ago   \\nFavorite  <::before> Select  [ Talk  Share  Actions  ](/index.php/apps/files?dir=//Talk) |  0 KB  |  a year ago   \\nFavorite  <::before> Select  [ Templates  Share  Actions  ](/index.php/apps/files?dir=//Templates) |  10.2 MB  |  a minute ago   \\nFavorite  <::before> Select  [ ownCloud Manual  .pdf  Share  Actions  ](/remote.php/webdav/ownCloud%20Manual.pdf) |  4.7 MB  |  a minute ago   \\n5 folders  and  1 file  (including 0 hidden)  |  86.9 MB  |   \\n  \\nThe files you are trying to upload exceed the maximum size for file uploads on this server. \\n\\n##  No favorites \\n\\nFiles and folders you mark as favorite will show up here \\n\\n##  No entries found in this folder \\n\\nName  |  Size  |  Modified  [ Delete  ]()  \\n---|---|---  \\n  \\n##  No entries found in this folder \\n\\nName  |  State  |  Share time  |  Expiration date   \\n---|---|---|---  \\n  \\n##  No entries found in this folder \\n\\nName  |  State  |  Share time  |  Expiration date   \\n---|---|---|---  \\n  \\n##  No entries found in this folder \\n\\nName  |  State  |  Share time  |  Expiration date   \\n---|---|---|---  \\n  \\n##  No files in here \\n\\n##  No entries found in this folder \\n\\nName  |  Size  |  Modified   \\n---|---|---  \\n  \\n##  No deleted files \\n\\nYou will be able to recover deleted files from here \\n\\n##  No entries found in this folder \\n\\nSelect all  Name  [ Restore  ]() |  Deleted  [ Delete  ]()  \\n---|---  \\n  \\n|   \\n---|---  \\n  \\n#  A safe home for all your data \\n\\nAccess & share your files, calendars, contacts, mail & more from any device, on your terms \\n\\n##  Get the apps to sync your files \\n\\n[ ](https://owncloud.org/install/#install-clients) [ ](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.owncloud.android) [ ](https://itunes.apple.com/us/app/owncloud/id543672169?mt=8)\\n\\n##  Connect your desktop apps to ownCloud \\n\\n[ Connect your Calendar ](https://doc.owncloud.org/server/10.0/go.php?to=user-sync-calendars) [ Connect your Contacts ](https://doc.owncloud.org/server/10.0/go.php?to=user-sync-contacts) [ Access files via WebDAV ](https://doc.owncloud.org/server/10.0/go.php?to=user-webdav)\\n\\n\u00a9 2025 [ ownCloud ](https://owncloud.org)\\n\\nclose \\n', url='http://the-agent-company.com:8092/index.php/apps/files/?dir=/&fileid=5', trigger_by_action='browse', error=False, observation='browse', goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['http://the-agent-company.com:8092/index.php/apps/files/?dir=/&fileid=5'], active_page_index=0, last_browser_action='goto(\"http://the-agent-company.com:8092/\")', last_browser_action_error='', focused_element_bid='747'), **FileEditAction**\nPath: [/workspace/engineering_policy.md]\nThought: \nCommand: create\nCreated File with Text:\n```\n# Engineering Policy\n\nPurpose: Set clear, high-performance expectations and ways of working so teams deliver results on time with quality, accountability, and respect.\n\nScope: Applies to all engineering employees and contractors.\n\n## Performance Expectations\nWe operate with urgency and demand excellence. Engineers are expected to:\n- Deliver on commitments on time; proactively surface risks early and propose mitigation.\n- Take end-to-end ownership of outcomes, not just tasks; hold yourself and your team accountable.\n- Maintain high quality: readable, tested, secure, and observable code.\n- Continuously improve skills, systems, and processes.\n- Communicate clearly, concisely, and respectfully; default to transparency.\n\nMeasures of performance include delivery predictability, business/customer impact, code quality and reliability, collaboration, and growth. Teams should use quarterly Objectives and Key Results (OKRs) and track leading indicators (cycle time, change failure rate, MTTR, test coverage).\n\nPerformance concerns are addressed through timely feedback and clear improvement plans. Repeated failure to meet expectations may lead to formal remediation per HR policy.\n\n## Team Conduct and Inclusion\nWe foster psychological safety and a culture of constructive challenge.\n- Treat everyone with respect; zero tolerance for harassment or discrimination.\n- Disagree and commit once decisions are made.\n- Uphold the Company Code of Conduct and escalate concerns via designated channels.\n\n## Ways of Working\n- Core collaboration window: 10:00\u201315:00 in each team\u2019s primary time zone. Outside this, work flexibly and asynchronously.\n- Meetings are purposeful with agendas and notes. Prefer written updates over status meetings.\n- Remote/hybrid: Be responsive during core hours; document decisions in shared systems.\n\n## Delivery Practices\n- Planning: Maintain a prioritized backlog; size work to ship incrementally.\n- Code review: All changes via pull requests with at least one reviewer; reviewers focus on correctness, simplicity, security, and tests.\n- Testing: Unit tests for new logic, integration tests for critical paths; aim for risk-based coverage and automation.\n- CI/CD: Every PR must pass automated checks; main is always releasable.\n- Releases and change management: Use tagged releases; follow rollback procedures; update changelogs and runbooks.\n- Observability: Emit metrics, logs, and traces; set SLOs/SLIs; respond to alerts.\n- Security and privacy: Follow secure coding practices, secret management, dependency scanning, and data handling standards; report vulnerabilities immediately.\n\n## Accountability and Decision-Making\n- Commitments are explicit with owners and due dates. If dates are at risk, escalate early.\n- Use lightweight RACI for significant decisions; record context and outcomes in an ADR or decision log.\n- Exceptions to policy require documented justification and approval from the relevant director.\n\n## Incident Response and On-Call\n- Each service has an on-call rotation, runbook, and escalation path.\n- Declare incidents promptly, communicate clearly, and conduct blameless postmortems with actionable follow-ups.\n\n## Career Growth\n- Regular 1:1s include feedback, goals, and development plans.\n- Promotions follow the leveling framework and evidence from impact, scope, and behaviors.\n- Learning: Use the team\u2019s learning budget for courses, books, and conferences.\n\n## Work Hours and Overtime\n- We value balance, but during critical milestones, short periods of extended effort may be required. Plan proactively to minimize overtime.\n- Overtime must be manager-approved and compliant with local laws. Compensation may be time off or bonuses per HR policy.\n\n## Documentation and Tooling\n- Keep documentation current in the designated knowledge base; PRs must update docs as needed.\n- Use approved tools for source control, CI/CD, monitoring, and ticketing; propose changes via an ADR.\n\n## Policy Review\nThis policy is reviewed at least annually by Engineering Leadership. Suggestions for improvement are welcome at any time.\n```\n, FileEditObservation(content='File created successfully at: /workspace/engineering_policy.md', path='/workspace/engineering_policy.md', prev_exist=False, old_content=None, new_content=None, observation='edit', impl_source='oh_aci', diff='--- /workspace/engineering_policy.md\\n+++ /workspace/engineering_policy.md\\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\\n+# Engineering Policy\\n@@ -1,0 +3,60 @@\\n+Purpose: Set clear, high-performance expectations and ways of working so teams deliver results on time with quality, accountability, and respect.\\n+\\n+Scope: Applies to all engineering employees and contractors.\\n+\\n+## Performance Expectations\\n+We operate with urgency and demand excellence. Engineers are expected to:\\n+- Deliver on commitments on time; proactively surface risks early and propose mitigation.\\n+- Take end-to-end ownership of outcomes, not just tasks; hold yourself and your team accountable.\\n+- Maintain high quality: readable, tested, secure, and observable code.\\n+- Continuously improve skills, systems, and processes.\\n+- Communicate clearly, concisely, and respectfully; default to transparency.\\n+\\n+Measures of performance include delivery predictability, business/customer impact, code quality and reliability, collaboration, and growth. Teams should use quarterly Objectives and Key Results (OKRs) and track leading indicators (cycle time, change failure rate, MTTR, test coverage).\\n+\\n+Performance concerns are addressed through timely feedback and clear improvement plans. Repeated failure to meet expectations may lead to formal remediation per HR policy.\\n+\\n+## Team Conduct and Inclusion\\n+We foster psychological safety and a culture of constructive challenge.\\n+- Treat everyone with respect; zero tolerance for harassment or discrimination.\\n+- Disagree and commit once decisions are made.\\n+- Uphold the Company Code of Conduct and escalate concerns via designated channels.\\n+\\n+## Ways of Working\\n+- Core collaboration window: 10:00\u201315:00 in each team\u2019s primary time zone. Outside this, work flexibly and asynchronously.\\n+- Meetings are purposeful with agendas and notes. Prefer written updates over status meetings.\\n+- Remote/hybrid: Be responsive during core hours; document decisions in shared systems.\\n+\\n+## Delivery Practices\\n+- Planning: Maintain a prioritized backlog; size work to ship incrementally.\\n+- Code review: All changes via pull requests with at least one reviewer; reviewers focus on correctness, simplicity, security, and tests.\\n+- Testing: Unit tests for new logic, integration tests for critical paths; aim for risk-based coverage and automation.\\n+- CI/CD: Every PR must pass automated checks; main is always releasable.\\n+- Releases and change management: Use tagged releases; follow rollback procedures; update changelogs and runbooks.\\n+- Observability: Emit metrics, logs, and traces; set SLOs/SLIs; respond to alerts.\\n+- Security and privacy: Follow secure coding practices, secret management, dependency scanning, and data handling standards; report vulnerabilities immediately.\\n+\\n+## Accountability and Decision-Making\\n+- Commitments are explicit with owners and due dates. If dates are at risk, escalate early.\\n+- Use lightweight RACI for significant decisions; record context and outcomes in an ADR or decision log.\\n+- Exceptions to policy require documented justification and approval from the relevant director.\\n+\\n+## Incident Response and On-Call\\n+- Each service has an on-call rotation, runbook, and escalation path.\\n+- Declare incidents promptly, communicate clearly, and conduct blameless postmortems with actionable follow-ups.\\n+\\n+## Career Growth\\n+- Regular 1:1s include feedback, goals, and development plans.\\n+- Promotions follow the leveling framework and evidence from impact, scope, and behaviors.\\n+- Learning: Use the team\u2019s learning budget for courses, books, and conferences.\\n+\\n+## Work Hours and Overtime\\n+- We value balance, but during critical milestones, short periods of extended effort may be required. Plan proactively to minimize overtime.\\n+- Overtime must be manager-approved and compliant with local laws. Compensation may be time off or bonuses per HR policy.\\n+\\n+## Documentation and Tooling\\n+- Keep documentation current in the designated knowledge base; PRs must update docs as needed.\\n+- Use approved tools for source control, CI/CD, monitoring, and ticketing; propose changes via an ADR.\\n+\\n+## Policy Review\\n+This policy is reviewed at least annually by Engineering Leadership. Suggestions for improvement are welcome at any time.', _diff_cache=None), BrowseInteractiveAction(browser_actions=\"goto('http://the-agent-company.com:8092/')\\nnoop()\", thought='', browsergym_send_msg_to_user='', action='browse_interactive', security_risk=None), BrowserOutputObservation(content='This application requires JavaScript for correct operation. Please [ enable JavaScript ](http://enable-javascript.com/) and reload the page. \\n\\n[ ownCloud 10.1.1 is available. Get mor